ect follows Semantic Versioning."},"28":{"id":"/en/changelog-26","page_id":"/en/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/changelog","content":"See Project History for the reasoning behind each release."},"29":{"id":"/en/changelog-27","page_id":"/en/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/changelog#added","content":"Visible top-right developer dock with vector cheat/terminal icons, drag grip, safe-area clamping and retained position across visibility changes and screen resizing."},"30":{"id":"/en/changelog-28","page_id":"/en/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/changelog#added","content":"Cheat parameter forms generated from usage: required/optional fields, choice buttons, grouped coordinates, rest arguments, validation and retained input values. Run buttons assemble and execute commands without typing their names."},"31":{"id":"/en/changelog-29","page_id":"/en/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/changelog#added","content":"Category filters and per-card execution feedback, including errors. Terminal now has a Run button, Tab completion, keyboard history, command echo and a safe-area layout."},"32":{"id":"/en/changelog-30","page_id":"/en/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/changelog#added","content":"Local cheat-authoring skills under `.agents/skills/cheat-terminal` and `.claude/skills/cheat-terminal`."},"33":{"id":"/en/changelog-31","page_id":"/en/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/changelog#added","content":"Unity tests for command forms, quoted values, execution, UI interaction, dock dragging and pause restoration."},"34":{"id":"/en/changelog-32","page_id":"/en/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/changelog#changed","content":"Default shortcuts are **F1: Cheat Library**, **F2: Terminal**. F10 remains a cheat shortcut; F9 toggles the dock; backquote opens Terminal; Escape closes the active surface. `ConsoleKey` and the new `CheatHudKey` are configurable."},"35":{"id":"/en/changelog-33","page_id":"/en/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/changelog#changed","content":"Redesigned both surfaces with consistent dark colors, mint accents, clearer spacing and dedicated controls. Switching surfaces closes the previous one while retaining aggregate visibility/pause behavior."},"36":{"id":"/en/changelog-34","page_id":"/en/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/changelog#changed","content":"Cheats run through explicit Run buttons; parameter forms are always visible. No additional registration is needed."},"37":{"id":"/en/changelog-35","page_id":"/en/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/changelog#changed","content":"Previous release entries are numbered `1.0.0` through `1.0.4`; this UI update is `1.1.0`."},"38":{"id":"/en/changelog-36","page_id":"/en/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/changelog#fixed","content":"Quoted argument serialization preserves spaces, embedded quotes, backslashes and empty quoted tokens."},"39":{"id":"/en/changelog-37","page_id":"/en/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/changelog#fixed","content":"HUD execution feedback reflects command errors instead of reporting every invocation as successful."},"40":{"id":"/en/changelog-38","page_id":"/en/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/changelog#fixed","content":"Generated dock icons and panel backgrounds include their required CanvasRenderer. Parameter fields retain their minimum height and no longer overlap Run buttons without a theme asset."},"41":{"id":"/en/changelog-39","page_id":"/en/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/changelog#changed-1","content":"The cheat HUD covers the whole screen instead of sliding in from the left. Rows are proper touch targets (104px minimum), content is inset by `Screen.safeArea`, wide screens split the list into two or three columns, and the bottom bar carries a large `CLOSE` button. The old panel is still available through `TerminalBehaviour.CheatHudFullScreen = false` and `CheatHudView.WidthPercent`."},"42":{"id":"/en/changelog-40","page_id":"/en/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/changelog#added-1","content":"Open/close listeners: `TerminalBehaviour.VisibilityChanged` (console and HUD combined), `ConsoleVisibilityChanged`, `CheatHudVisibilityChanged`. The views raise `OnOpened` / `OnClosed` / `OnVisibilityChanged` directly."},"43":{"id":"/en/changelog-41","page_id":"/en/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/changelog#added-1","content":"`TerminalBehaviour.PauseGameWhileOpen` / `PausedTimeScale`: hold `Time.timeScale` while open and restore it on close."},"44":{"id":"/en/changelog-42","page_id":"/en/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/changelog#added-1","content":"Console keyboard shortcuts for the editor and desktop: `F1` toggles, the backquote `` ` `` only opens (so it never eats a keystroke while typing). The cheat HUD also answers to `F2` next to `F10`."},"45":{"id":"/en/changelog-43","page_id":"/en/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/changelog#added-1","content":"`Tools > Cheat Terminal` editor menu for play mode (toggle console / HUD / handle, Pause Game While Open, manual bootstrap)."},"46":{"id":"/en/changelog-44","page_id":"/en/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/changelog#added-1","content":"`TerminalShortcutKey` gained `F1`-`F4`, `F11`, `F12`, `BackQuote`, `Escape`; `MultiFingerTapGesture` accepts a second `AlternateKey`."},"47":{"id":"/en/changelog-45","page_id":"/en/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/changelog#fixed-1","content":"Input System-only projects had no `EventSystem`, leaving every console and cheat HUD button dead. One is now created with `InputSystemUIInputModule`."},"48":{"id":"/en/changelog-46","page_id":"/en/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/changelog#documentation","content":"Added a Project History page reconstructed from the commit history (ko / en / ja / zh)."},"49":{"id":"/en/changelog-47","page_id":"/en/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/changelog#changed-2","content":"The top-right `>_` handle is hidden by default. Tapping with **four fingers three times** anywhere on screen shows it, and the same gesture hides it again. `TerminalCornerTrigger.Visible` / `TerminalBehaviour.HandleVisible` expose it from code (`TerminalCornerTrigger.Enabled` is kept as an alias)."},"50":{"id":"/en/changelog-48","page_id":"/en/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/changelog#added-2","content":"Cheat HUD (`CheatHudView`): a UI Toolkit panel that slides in from the left and lists every registered command, grouped by category. Toggled by tapping with **three fingers three times** (F10 on desktop) or through `TerminalBehaviour.Open/Close/ToggleCheatHud()`. Cheats without arguments run on a single tap; cheats with `<...>` or `[...]` arguments open an inline input. Includes a search box, a status line for the last executed command, and a `>_` button that opens the console."},"51":{"id":"/en/changelog-49","page_id":"/en/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/changelog#added-2","content":"`MultiFingerTapGesture`: reusable \"N fingers, M taps\" detector that requires an exact finger count, so the three- and four-finger gestures never trigger each other. Optional keyboard fallback (F9 / F10) for the editor and desktop."},"52":{"id":"/en/changelog-50","page_id":"/en/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/changelog#added-2","content":"`TerminalInput`: reflection-free input abstraction covering both the legacy Input Manager and the Input System package."},"53":{"id":"/en/changelog-51","page_id":"/en/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/changelog#added-2","content":"`AGENT.md` documenting the conventions for authoring cheats."},"54":{"id":"/en/changelog-52","page_id":"/en/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/changelog#changed-breaking","content":"Removed reflection-based `[Terminal]` method discovery and invocation. Commands are now registered explicitly with `RegisterCommand(...)`."},"55":{"id":"/en/changelog-53","page_id":"/en/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/changelog#changed-breaking","content":"Removed the reflection-based Object Inspector module from the default runtime."},"56":{"id":"/en/changelog-54","page_id":"/en/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/changelog#changed-breaking","content":"EventSystem fallback no longer probes optional Input System types via reflection. Projects using Input System-only input should provide an EventSystem with `InputSystemUIInputModule`."},"57":{"id":"/en/changelog-55","page_id":"/en/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/changelog#fixed-2","content":"Terminal input now executes only on an explicit submit, not on focus loss."},"58":{"id":"/en/changelog-56","page_id":"/en/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/changelog#fixed-2","content":"Terminal output escapes rich text-sensitive characters before wrapping lines in color tags."},"59":{"id":"/en/changelog-57","page_id":"/en/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/changelog#fixed-2","content":"Unity component commands now use invariant-culture numeric parsing, strict bool parsing, and inactive-inclusive GameObject lookup where appropriate."},"60":{"id":"/en/changelog-58","page_id":"/en/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/changelog#fixed-2","content":"Runtime helper GameObjects created by Logs and Performance modules are disposed with the terminal bootstrap."},"61":{"id":"/en/changelog-59","page_id":"/en/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/changelog#added-3","content":"Cached completion items for command names, usage keywords, and command-specific providers."},"62":{"id":"/en/changelog-60","page_id":"/en/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/changelog#added-3","content":"Context-aware completions for built-in commands, including scenes, logs, GameObjects, component targets, and boolean values."},"63":{"id":"/en/changelog-61","page_id":"/en/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/changelog#added-3","content":"`data [table] [id|text]` command plus `RegisterDataTable(...)` for reflection-free data lookup."},"64":{"id":"/en/changelog-62","page_id":"/en/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/changelog#added-3","content":"Terminal UI tabs for Console, registered Commands, and registered Data tables."},"65":{"id":"/en/changelog-63","page_id":"/en/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/changelog#changed-3","content":"Renamed the namespace from `UniTerminal` to `Achieve.CheatTerminal`."},"66":{"id":"/en/changelog-64","page_id":"/en/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/changelog#added-4","content":"Unity component commands: `transform`, `rb`, `cam`, `light`, `audio`, `time`, `go`."},"67":{"id":"/en/changelog-65","page_id":"/en/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/changelog#added-4","content":"Documentation in Korean, English, Japanese and Chinese, including advanced module usage."},"68":{"id":"/en/changelog-66","page_id":"/en/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/changelog#changed-breaking-1","content":"Removed the internal collaborator interfaces (`ICommandRegistry`, `ICommandParser`, `ICommandHistory`, `IAutoCompleteProvider`, `IAliasResolver`, `IArgumentConverter`, `ITerminalTrigger`, `ITerminal`) and `TerminalBuilder`. The core `Terminal` is now a concrete class that owns concrete collaborators. Only `ICommand`, `ICommandOutput`, `ITerminalView`, and `ITerminalModule` remain as real extension points."},"69":{"id":"/en/changelog-67","page_id":"/en/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/changelog#changed-breaking-1","content":"No marker interface for commands - the `[Terminal]` attribute is the only marker."},"70":{"id":"/en/changelog-68","page_id":"/en/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/changelog#changed-breaking-1","content":"`Terminal.ScanStaticCommands()` scans user assemblies and auto-registers all static `[Terminal]` methods. The bootstrap runs it on startup through `TerminalBehaviour.AutoScanStaticCommands`. Instance commands still use `Register(this)`."},"71":{"id":"/en/changelog-69","page_id":"/en/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/changelog#added-5","content":"Runtime Logs module: captures `Debug.Log` output into a ring buffer with `logs [n | error | warning | info | <text> | find <text> | clear | export]`. Export writes to `Application.persistentDataPath` so logs are retrievable on device."},"72":{"id":"/en/changelog-70","page_id":"/en/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/changelog#added-5","content":"Up/Down arrow recalls previous/next command history in the input field via uGUI `IMoveHandler`, so it works under both the legacy Input Manager and the Input System package."},"73":{"id":"/en/changelog-71","page_id":"/en/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/changelog#added-5","content":"`help <category>` lists the commands in a category with descriptions. `help` now hints at `help <command>` / `help <category>`."},"74":{"id":"/en/changelog-72","page_id":"/en/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/changelog#fixed-3","content":"EventSystem now creates `InputSystemUIInputModule` when the Input System package is active, resolved via reflection, avoiding the per-frame `InvalidOperationException`."},"75":{"id":"/en/changelog-73","page_id":"/en/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/changelog#fixed-3","content":"Top-right corner trigger is now a visible `>_` handle and opens on a single tap."},"76":{"id":"/en/changelog-74","page_id":"/en/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/changelog#added-6","content":"Core command system: `ICommandRegistry`, `ICommandParser` (quote-aware), `ICommandHistory`, `IAutoCompleteProvider`, `IAliasResolver`, `IArgumentConverter`, and `ICommandOutput` with default implementations."},"77":{"id":"/en/changelog-75","page_id":"/en/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/changelog#added-6","content":"`[Terminal(\"name {0}\")]` attribute and reflection-based `AttributeCommand` binding, including positional binding, optional parameters, and `CommandContext` injection."},"78":{"id":"/en/changelog-76","page_id":"/en/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/changelog#added-6","content":"Interface-driven `Terminal` core assembled via `TerminalBuilder`."},"79":{"id":"/en/changelog-77","page_id":"/en/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/changelog#added-6","content":"uGUI overlay view (`UGuiTerminalView`) deactivated while closed for zero idle cost."},"80":{"id":"/en/changelog-78","page_id":"/en/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/changelog#added-6","content":"Top-right corner open gesture (`TerminalCornerTrigger`, double-tap by default)."},"81":{"id":"/en/changelog-79","page_id":"/en/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/changelog#added-6","content":"`TerminalBehaviour` bootstrap with a static convenience API. It auto-bootstraps in the editor and development builds."},"82":{"id":"/en/changelog-80","page_id":"/en/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/changelog#added-6","content":"Built-in commands: `help`, `clear`, `history`, `echo`, `alias`."},"83":{"id":"/en/changelog-81","page_id":"/en/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/changelog#added-6","content":"Module system (`ITerminalModule`) with `InstallModule` / `GetModule<T>` on the bootstrap."},"84":{"id":"/en/changelog-82","page_id":"/en/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/changelog#added-6","content":"Scene Tools module: `scene list | load <name> [additive] | unload <name>`."},"85":{"id":"/en/changelog-83","page_id":"/en/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/changelog#added-6","content":"Object Inspector module: `find`, `inspect`, `set <name>.<member> <value>`, `call`, with explicit object registration (`ObjectInspectorModule.RegisterObject`)."},"86":{"id":"/en/changelog-84","page_id":"/en/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/changelog#added-6","content":"Performance Monitor module: `perf` (FPS, frame ms, memory, GC, render stats via `ProfilerRecorder`)."},"87":{"id":"/en/changelog-85","page_id":"/en/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/changelog#added-6","content":"Basic Usage sample."},"88":{"id":"/en/getting-started","page_id":"/en/getting-started","type":"page","content":"Getting Started","breadcrumbs":["Docs"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/getting-started"},"89":{"id":"/en/getting-started-0","page_id":"/en/getting-started","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/getting-started#installation","content":"Installation"},"90":{"id":"/en/getting-started-1","page_id":"/en/getting-started","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/getting-started#opening-the-console","content":"Opening the console"},"91":{"id":"/en/getting-started-2","page_id":"/en/getting-started","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/getting-started#using-it-in-the-editor","content":"Using it in the editor"},"92":{"id":"/en/getting-started-3","page_id":"/en/getting-started","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/getting-started#control-from-code","content":"Control from code"},"93":{"id":"/en/getting-started-4","page_id":"/en/getting-started","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/getting-started#parameter-forms-and-execution","content":"Parameter forms and execution"},"94":{"id":"/en/getting-started-5","page_id":"/en/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/getting-started#installation","content":"In Unity Package Manager, choose **Add package from git URL**:"},"95":{"id":"/en/getting-started-6","page_id":"/en/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/getting-started#opening-the-console","content":"The terminal bootstraps automatically in the editor and development builds. A developer dock is visible at the top right: the sliders icon opens Cheat Library and the terminal icon opens Terminal. Drag the grip or either icon to move the dock within the safe area."},"96":{"id":"/en/getting-started-7","page_id":"/en/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/getting-started#opening-the-console","content":"Action"},"97":{"id":"/en/getting-started-8","page_id":"/en/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/getting-started#opening-the-console","content":"How"},"98":{"id":"/en/getting-started-9","page_id":"/en/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/getting-started#opening-the-console","content":"Editor / desktop"},"99":{"id":"/en/getting-started-10","page_id":"/en/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/getting-started#opening-the-console","content":"Show / hide the top-right `Terminal` handle"},"100":{"id":"/en/getting-started-11","page_id":"/en/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/getting-started#opening-the-console","content":"**Tap with 4 fingers, 3 times**"},"101":{"id":"/en/getting-started-12","page_id":"/en/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/getting-started#opening-the-console","content":"`F9`"},"102":{"id":"/en/getting-started-13","page_id":"/en/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/getting-started#opening-the-console","content":"Open / close the cheat HUD"},"103":{"id":"/en/getting-started-14","page_id":"/en/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/getting-started#opening-the-console","content":"**Tap with 3 fingers, 3 times**"},"104":{"id":"/en/getting-started-15","page_id":"/en/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/getting-started#opening-the-console","content":"`F1`, `F10`"},"105":{"id":"/en/getting-started-16","page_id":"/en/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/getting-started#opening-the-console","content":"Open / close the console"},"106":{"id":"/en/getting-started-17","page_id":"/en/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/getting-started#opening-the-console","content":"Tap the `Terminal` handle, or the panel `Close`"},"107":{"id":"/en/getting-started-18","page_id":"/en/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/getting-started#opening-the-console","content":"`F2`, `` ` ``"},"108":{"id":"/en/getting-started-19","page_id":"/en/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/getting-started#opening-the-console","content":"Run a command"},"109":{"id":"/en/getting-started-20","page_id":"/en/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/getting-started#opening-the-console","content":"Type and press Enter"},"110":{"id":"/en/getting-started-21","page_id":"/en/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/getting-started#opening-the-console","content":"Previous / next history"},"111":{"id":"/en/getting-started-22","page_id":"/en/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/getting-started#opening-the-console","content":"Up / Down arrow"},"112":{"id":"/en/getting-started-23","page_id":"/en/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/getting-started#opening-the-console","content":"Help"},"113":{"id":"/en/getting-started-24","page_id":"/en/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/getting-started#opening-the-console","content":"`help`, `help <category>`, `help <command>`"},"114":{"id":"/en/getting-started-25","page_id":"/en/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/getting-started#opening-the-console","content":"Repeating the same gesture closes it again. See Cheat HUD for details."},"115":{"id":"/en/getting-started-26","page_id":"/en/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/getting-started#using-it-in-the-editor","content":"A mouse cannot produce a multi-touch gesture, so the editor and desktop use keys instead:\n`F1` opens Cheat Library, `F2` opens Terminal, `F10` is another cheat shortcut, and `F9` toggles the dock. Backquote only opens Terminal; Escape closes the active surface."},"116":{"id":"/en/getting-started-27","page_id":"/en/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/getting-started#using-it-in-the-editor","content":"When the Game view does not have focus the keys never reach the game. Use the menu then:"},"117":{"id":"/en/getting-started-28","page_id":"/en/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/getting-started#using-it-in-the-editor","content":"Nothing is clickable without an `EventSystem`. If the scene has none, the terminal creates\none - with `InputSystemUIInputModule` in Input System-only projects."},"118":{"id":"/en/getting-started-29","page_id":"/en/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/getting-started#parameter-forms-and-execution","content":"Parameter fields are always visible. Enter values and press Run or Enter; you never need to type the command name. `<amount>` is required, `[amount]` is optional, `<x> <y> <z>` creates separate coordinate fields, and `<on|off>` adds choice buttons. Required fields must be filled. Optional fields can be omitted from the end, without gaps. `[args]` and `<text...>` accept several space-separated arguments; quote a single value that contains spaces."},"119":{"id":"/en/getting-started-30","page_id":"/en/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/getting-started#parameter-forms-and-execution","content":"Use category buttons and search to find commands. Values survive filtering, resizing and reopening. Results and errors appear on the card, bottom status bar and terminal output. Switching surfaces closes the previous surface."},"120":{"id":"/en/getting-started-31","page_id":"/en/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/getting-started#parameter-forms-and-execution","content":"Next: Adding Commands"},"121":{"id":"/en/history","page_id":"/en/history","type":"page","content":"Project History","breadcrumbs":["Docs"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/history"},"122":{"id":"/en/history-0","page_id":"/en/history","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/history#at-a-glance","content":"At a glance"},"123":{"id":"/en/history-1","page_id":"/en/history","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/history#three-turning-points","content":"Three turning points"},"124":{"id":"/en/history-2","page_id":"/en/history","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/history#103--gestures-and-the-cheat-hud","content":"1.0.3 — Gestures and the cheat HUD"},"125":{"id":"/en/history-3","page_id":"/en/history","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/history#102--reflection-removed-completion-sharpened","content":"1.0.2 — Reflection removed, completion sharpened"},"126":{"id":"/en/history-4","page_id":"/en/history","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/history#101--namespace-and-unity-component-commands","content":"1.0.1 — Namespace and Unity component commands"},"127":{"id":"/en/history-5","page_id":"/en/history","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/history#100--rewritten-around-a-concrete-core","content":"1.0.0 — Rewritten around a concrete core"},"128":{"id":"/en/history-6","page_id":"/en/history","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/history#010--first-release","content":"0.1.0 — First release"},"129":{"id":"/en/history-7","page_id":"/en/history","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/history#upgrade-cheat-sheet","content":"Upgrade cheat sheet"},"130":{"id":"/en/history-8","page_id":"/en/history","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/history","content":"How this package evolved, reconstructed from its commit history. The\nChangelog records *what* changed in each release; this page records *why*."},"131":{"id":"/en/history-9","page_id":"/en/history","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/history#at-a-glance","content":"Version"},"132":{"id":"/en/history-10","page_id":"/en/history","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/history#at-a-glance","content":"Date"},"133":{"id":"/en/history-11","page_id":"/en/history","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/history#at-a-glance","content":"Headline change"},"134":{"id":"/en/history-12","page_id":"/en/history","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/history#at-a-glance","content":"1.1.0"},"135":{"id":"/en/history-13","page_id":"/en/history","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/history#at-a-glance","content":"2026-10-17"},"136":{"id":"/en/history-14","page_id":"/en/history","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/history#at-a-glance","content":"Parameter forms, draggable dock, F1/F2 shortcuts and execution feedback"},"137":{"id":"/en/history-15","page_id":"/en/history","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/history#at-a-glance","content":"1.0.4"},"138":{"id":"/en/history-16","page_id":"/en/history","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/history#at-a-glance","content":"2026-08-29"},"139":{"id":"/en/history-17","page_id":"/en/history","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/history#at-a-glance","content":"Full-screen cheat HUD, visibility events and editor support"},"140":{"id":"/en/history-18","page_id":"/en/history","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/history#at-a-glance","content":"1.0.3"},"141":{"id":"/en/history-19","page_id":"/en/history","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/history#at-a-glance","content":"2026-08-17"},"142":{"id":"/en/history-20","page_id":"/en/history","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/history#at-a-glance","content":"Multi-touch gestures bring the UI up; UI Toolkit cheat HUD"},"143":{"id":"/en/history-21","page_id":"/en/history","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/history#at-a-glance","content":"1.0.2"},"144":{"id":"/en/history-22","page_id":"/en/history","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/history#at-a-glance","content":"2026-06-27"},"145":{"id":"/en/history-23","page_id":"/en/history","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/history#at-a-glance","content":"Reflection removed for good, context-aware completion, data tables"},"146":{"id":"/en/history-24","page_id":"/en/history","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/history#at-a-glance","content":"1.0.1"},"147":{"id":"/en/history-25","page_id":"/en/history","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/history#at-a-glance","content":"2026-05-30"},"148":{"id":"/en/history-26","page_id":"/en/history","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/history#at-a-glance","content":"`Achieve.CheatTerminal` namespace, Unity component commands"},"149":{"id":"/en/history-27","page_id":"/en/history","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/history#at-a-glance","content":"1.0.0"},"150":{"id":"/en/history-28","page_id":"/en/history","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/history#at-a-glance","content":"2026-05-29"},"151":{"id":"/en/history-29","page_id":"/en/history","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/history#at-a-glance","content":"Rewritten around a concrete core, Logs module"},"152":{"id":"/en/history-30","page_id":"/en/history","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/history#at-a-glance","content":"0.1.0"},"153":{"id":"/en/history-31","page_id":"/en/history","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/history#at-a-glance","content":"2026-05-29"},"154":{"id":"/en/history-32","page_id":"/en/history","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/history#at-a-glance","content":"First core, uGUI view, module system"},"155":{"id":"/en/history-33","page_id":"/en/history","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/history#three-turning-points","content":"**Reflection → explicit registration.** 0.1.0 discovered commands through a\n`[Terminal(\"name {0}\")]` attribute and reflection binding, and 1.0.0 added automatic\nscanning of static methods on top. To keep runtime behavior predictable under IL2CPP/AOT,\n1.0.2 removed the attribute, the scan and every reflective call path, leaving explicit\n`RegisterCommand(...)` as the only way in."},"156":{"id":"/en/history-34","page_id":"/en/history","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/history#three-turning-points","content":"**Interface zoo → concrete core.** The collaborator interfaces of 0.1.0\n(`ICommandRegistry`, `ICommandParser`, `IAutoCompleteProvider`, …) and `TerminalBuilder`\nwere deleted in 1.0.0; `Terminal` now owns concrete collaborators directly. Only\n`ICommand`, `ICommandOutput`, `ITerminalView` and `ITerminalModule` remain as extension\npoints."},"157":{"id":"/en/history-35","page_id":"/en/history","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/history#three-turning-points","content":"**Always-on UI → gesture-summoned UI.** The invisible double-tap corner area of 0.1.0\nbecame a visible single-tap `>_` handle in 1.0.0, and in 1.0.3 that handle itself became\nhidden by default, reachable only through a multi-touch gesture."},"158":{"id":"/en/history-36","page_id":"/en/history","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/history#103--gestures-and-the-cheat-hud","content":"The top-right `>_` handle is hidden by default; **four fingers tapped three times** shows\nand hides it."},"159":{"id":"/en/history-37","page_id":"/en/history","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/history#103--gestures-and-the-cheat-hud","content":"Added a **UI Toolkit cheat HUD** that slides in from the left. Every registered command is\nlisted automatically, grouped by category, and cheats without arguments run on a single tap.\n**Three fingers tapped three times** opens and closes it. → Cheat HUD"},"160":{"id":"/en/history-38","page_id":"/en/history","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/history#103--gestures-and-the-cheat-hud","content":"Gestures come from `MultiFingerTapGesture`, which requires an exact finger count so the\nthree- and four-finger gestures can never trigger each other."},"161":{"id":"/en/history-39","page_id":"/en/history","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/history#103--gestures-and-the-cheat-hud","content":"Touch reading goes through the `TerminalInput` abstraction, covering the legacy Input\nManager and the Input System package without reflection (the latter being an optional\ndependency resolved by a version define)."},"162":{"id":"/en/history-40","page_id":"/en/history","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/history#103--gestures-and-the-cheat-hud","content":"Added `AGENT.md` at the repository root with the conventions for authoring cheats."},"163":{"id":"/en/history-41","page_id":"/en/history","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/history#102--reflection-removed-completion-sharpened","content":"Deleted `TerminalAttribute`, `AttributeCommand` and the reflection-based Object Inspector\nmodule. Commands previously registered through the attribute must move to\n`RegisterCommand(...)`."},"164":{"id":"/en/history-42","page_id":"/en/history","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/history#102--reflection-removed-completion-sharpened","content":"Completion now caches command names, `usage` keywords and command-specific candidates, and\noffers context-aware suggestions for scenes, logs, GameObjects, component targets and\nboolean values (`ICommandCompletionProvider`, `CommandCompletionContext`, `CompletionItem`)."},"165":{"id":"/en/history-43","page_id":"/en/history","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/history#102--reflection-removed-completion-sharpened","content":"`RegisterDataTable(...)` and the `data [table] [id|text]` command expose game data tables\nwithout reflection."},"166":{"id":"/en/history-44","page_id":"/en/history","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/history#102--reflection-removed-completion-sharpened","content":"The terminal UI gained `Console / Commands / Data` tabs."},"167":{"id":"/en/history-45","page_id":"/en/history","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/history#102--reflection-removed-completion-sharpened","content":"Fixes: input runs only on an explicit submit rather than on focus loss, output escapes rich\ntext-sensitive characters, Unity component commands parse with invariant culture, and the\nhelper GameObjects created by the Logs and Performance modules are disposed with the\nbootstrap."},"168":{"id":"/en/history-46","page_id":"/en/history","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/history#102--reflection-removed-completion-sharpened","content":"Around the same time the documentation site moved from Docusaurus to **Fumadocs + Next.js**,\nthe folder was unified as `docs~`, the Introduction / Getting started / Usage / Changelog\nstructure was settled and a Korean `CHANGELOG.ko.md` was added."},"169":{"id":"/en/history-47","page_id":"/en/history","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/history#101--namespace-and-unity-component-commands","content":"Renamed the namespace `UniTerminal` → `Achieve.CheatTerminal` (breaking)."},"170":{"id":"/en/history-48","page_id":"/en/history","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/history#101--namespace-and-unity-component-commands","content":"Added commands that drive Unity's built-in components directly: `transform`, `rb`, `cam`,\n`light`, `audio`, `time`, `go`. → Unity component commands"},"171":{"id":"/en/history-49","page_id":"/en/history","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/history#101--namespace-and-unity-component-commands","content":"Localized the docs into ko / en / ja / zh, added the advanced `ITerminalModule` section and\nintroduced the `CHANGELOG`."},"172":{"id":"/en/history-50","page_id":"/en/history","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/history#100--rewritten-around-a-concrete-core","content":"Removed the collaborator interfaces and `TerminalBuilder`; `Terminal` became a concrete class."},"173":{"id":"/en/history-51","page_id":"/en/history","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/history#100--rewritten-around-a-concrete-core","content":"`Terminal.ScanStaticCommands()` auto-registered static `[Terminal]` methods (this was later\nremoved in 1.0.2)."},"174":{"id":"/en/history-52","page_id":"/en/history","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/history#100--rewritten-around-a-concrete-core","content":"**Runtime Logs module**: captures `Debug.Log` into a ring buffer, queried with\n`logs [n | error | warning | info | <text> | find <text> | clear | export]`. `export` writes\nto `Application.persistentDataPath`, so logs are retrievable from a device."},"175":{"id":"/en/history-53","page_id":"/en/history","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/history#100--rewritten-around-a-concrete-core","content":"Up/Down arrows recall command history in the input field, and `help <category>` was added."},"176":{"id":"/en/history-54","page_id":"/en/history","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/history#100--rewritten-around-a-concrete-core","content":"Fixed the EventSystem input module, turned the corner trigger into a visible `>_` handle with\na single tap, added Unity `.meta` files, and settled the package name\n`com.achieve.cheat-terminal`."},"177":{"id":"/en/history-55","page_id":"/en/history","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/history#100--rewritten-around-a-concrete-core","content":"Added the documentation site (Docusaurus) and CI that deploys it to GitHub Pages."},"178":{"id":"/en/history-56","page_id":"/en/history","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/history#010--first-release","content":"Core made of a quote-aware parser, history, aliases, argument conversion, completion and an\noutput buffer."},"179":{"id":"/en/history-57","page_id":"/en/history","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/history#010--first-release","content":"`[Terminal]` attribute binding through reflection, assembled with `TerminalBuilder`."},"180":{"id":"/en/history-58","page_id":"/en/history","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/history#010--first-release","content":"uGUI overlay view that is fully deactivated while closed, plus a double-tap corner trigger."},"181":{"id":"/en/history-59","page_id":"/en/history","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/history#010--first-release","content":"Built-in commands `help`, `clear`, `history`, `echo`, `alias`."},"182":{"id":"/en/history-60","page_id":"/en/history","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/history#010--first-release","content":"Module system (`ITerminalModule`) with Scene Tools, Object Inspector and Performance modules,\nand the Basic Usage sample."},"183":{"id":"/en/history-61","page_id":"/en/history","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/history#upgrade-cheat-sheet","content":"Was"},"184":{"id":"/en/history-62","page_id":"/en/history","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/history#upgrade-cheat-sheet","content":"Is"},"185":{"id":"/en/history-63","page_id":"/en/history","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/history#upgrade-cheat-sheet","content":"`[Terminal]` attribute / static scan"},"186":{"id":"/en/history-64","page_id":"/en/history","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/history#upgrade-cheat-sheet","content":"`TerminalBehaviour.RegisterCommand(...)`"},"187":{"id":"/en/history-65","page_id":"/en/history","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/history#upgrade-cheat-sheet","content":"`UniTerminal` namespace"},"188":{"id":"/en/history-66","page_id":"/en/history","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/history#upgrade-cheat-sheet","content":"`Achieve.CheatTerminal`"},"189":{"id":"/en/history-67","page_id":"/en/history","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/history#upgrade-cheat-sheet","content":"`TerminalBuilder` assembly"},"190":{"id":"/en/history-68","page_id":"/en/history","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/history#upgrade-cheat-sheet","content":"`new Terminal()` + `AttachView(...)`"},"191":{"id":"/en/history-69","page_id":"/en/history","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/history#upgrade-cheat-sheet","content":"Object Inspector module"},"192":{"id":"/en/history-70","page_id":"/en/history","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/history#upgrade-cheat-sheet","content":"`RegisterDataTable(...)` + the `data` command"},"193":{"id":"/en/history-71","page_id":"/en/history","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/history#upgrade-cheat-sheet","content":"Always-visible corner handle"},"194":{"id":"/en/history-72","page_id":"/en/history","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/history#upgrade-cheat-sheet","content":"Four-finger triple tap (`TerminalBehaviour.HandleVisible`)"},"195":{"id":"/en/history-73","page_id":"/en/history","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/history#upgrade-cheat-sheet","content":"`TerminalCornerTrigger.Enabled`"},"196":{"id":"/en/history-74","page_id":"/en/history","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/history#upgrade-cheat-sheet","content":"`TerminalCornerTrigger.Visible` (`Enabled` kept as an alias)"},"197":{"id":"/en","page_id":"/en","type":"page","content":"Introduction","breadcrumbs":["Docs"],"tags":[],"url":"/en"},"198":{"id":"/en-0","page_id":"/en","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en#features","content":"Features"},"199":{"id":"/en-1","page_id":"/en","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en#requirements","content":"Requirements"},"200":{"id":"/en-2","page_id":"/en","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en","content":"Cheat Terminal is a Unity runtime developer console for cheats, debugging, log review, and live runtime control."},"201":{"id":"/en-3","page_id":"/en","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en","content":"Commands are registered explicitly with `RegisterCommand(...)`. There is no automatic assembly scanning or reflection invocation in the default runtime path, which keeps IL2CPP/AOT builds predictable. The console runs as a uGUI overlay with **zero idle cost** while closed."},"202":{"id":"/en-4","page_id":"/en","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en#features","content":"**Explicit registration** - Register commands with `RegisterCommand(\"name\", ctx => ...)`; no hidden reflection scan."},"203":{"id":"/en-5","page_id":"/en","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en#features","content":"**Runtime IntelliSense** - Shows command, keyword, data table, and row suggestions with details."},"204":{"id":"/en-6","page_id":"/en","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en#features","content":"**Performance-first** - Disabled canvas while closed, capped output ring buffer, and keyboard history through the shared `TerminalInput` backend."},"205":{"id":"/en-7","page_id":"/en","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en#features","content":"**Modular** - Scene, Data, Performance, Logs, and Unity Components modules are installed by default."},"206":{"id":"/en-8","page_id":"/en","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en#features","content":"**Tabbed UI** - Console, Commands, and Data tabs show output, registered commands, and registered data."},"207":{"id":"/en-9","page_id":"/en","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en#features","content":"**Mobile-friendly** - Multi-touch gestures (3 or 4 fingers, tapped 3 times) bring the UI up, and device logs export to a file."},"208":{"id":"/en-10","page_id":"/en","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en#features","content":"**Cheat HUD** - Run registered cheats with parameter fields and Run buttons in a full-screen UI Toolkit panel; open/close listeners drive `Time.timeScale`."},"209":{"id":"/en-11","page_id":"/en","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en#requirements","content":"Unity 6 (6000.x)"},"210":{"id":"/en-12","page_id":"/en","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en#requirements","content":"`com.unity.ugui` (included by default)"},"211":{"id":"/en-13","page_id":"/en","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en#requirements","content":"Next: Getting Started"},"212":{"id":"/en/usage/adding-commands","page_id":"/en/usage/adding-commands","type":"page","content":"Adding Commands","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Usage"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/usage/adding-commands"},"213":{"id":"/en/usage/adding-commands-0","page_id":"/en/usage/adding-commands","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/usage/adding-commands#basic-registration","content":"Basic registration"},"214":{"id":"/en/usage/adding-commands-1","page_id":"/en/usage/adding-commands","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/usage/adding-commands#static-commands","content":"Static commands"},"215":{"id":"/en/usage/adding-commands-2","page_id":"/en/usage/adding-commands","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/usage/adding-commands#arguments","content":"Arguments"},"216":{"id":"/en/usage/adding-commands-3","page_id":"/en/usage/adding-commands","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/usage/adding-commands#adding-completion-candidates","content":"Adding completion candidates"},"217":{"id":"/en/usage/adding-commands-4","page_id":"/en/usage/adding-commands","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/usage/adding-commands#registering-data-tables","content":"Registering data tables"},"218":{"id":"/en/usage/adding-commands-5","page_id":"/en/usage/adding-commands","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/usage/adding-commands#writing-output","content":"Writing output"},"219":{"id":"/en/usage/adding-commands-6","page_id":"/en/usage/adding-commands","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/usage/adding-commands#advanced-iterminalmodule","content":"Advanced: ITerminalModule"},"220":{"id":"/en/usage/adding-commands-7","page_id":"/en/usage/adding-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/adding-commands","content":"Commands are registered explicitly with `RegisterCommand(...)`. There is no automatic scan, and execution uses a `CommandContext` delegate instead of reflection invocation."},"221":{"id":"/en/usage/adding-commands-8","page_id":"/en/usage/adding-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/adding-commands","content":"> **Usage string rules** — `usage` decides how the cheat runs in the cheat HUD.\n> Write no brackets when the command takes no arguments (`god`), `<amount>` for required\n> arguments and `[amount]` for optional ones. The HUD creates separate parameter fields and a Run button. You do not need to type the command name. → Cheat HUD"},"222":{"id":"/en/usage/adding-commands-9","page_id":"/en/usage/adding-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/adding-commands#basic-registration","content":"Run `gold 100000` or `god` in the console. `help Cheats` lists commands in that category with descriptions."},"223":{"id":"/en/usage/adding-commands-10","page_id":"/en/usage/adding-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/adding-commands#static-commands","content":"Static methods are not collected automatically. Register them explicitly when you want them available."},"224":{"id":"/en/usage/adding-commands-11","page_id":"/en/usage/adding-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/adding-commands#static-commands","content":"Register them with:"},"225":{"id":"/en/usage/adding-commands-12","page_id":"/en/usage/adding-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/adding-commands#arguments","content":"Read arguments from `CommandContext`."},"226":{"id":"/en/usage/adding-commands-13","page_id":"/en/usage/adding-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/adding-commands#arguments","content":"`ctx.Args`: raw argument list"},"227":{"id":"/en/usage/adding-commands-14","page_id":"/en/usage/adding-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/adding-commands#arguments","content":"`ctx.Has(index)`: whether an argument exists"},"228":{"id":"/en/usage/adding-commands-15","page_id":"/en/usage/adding-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/adding-commands#arguments","content":"`ctx.GetString/GetInt/GetFloat/GetBool`: fallback-based convenience getters"},"229":{"id":"/en/usage/adding-commands-16","page_id":"/en/usage/adding-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/adding-commands#arguments","content":"For strict validation, use `TryParse(..., CultureInfo.InvariantCulture, ...)` directly."},"230":{"id":"/en/usage/adding-commands-17","page_id":"/en/usage/adding-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/adding-commands#adding-completion-candidates","content":"You can attach command-specific suggestions at registration time."},"231":{"id":"/en/usage/adding-commands-18","page_id":"/en/usage/adding-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/adding-commands#adding-completion-candidates","content":"Usage tokens like `<easy|normal|hard>` are also cached as default keyword suggestions."},"232":{"id":"/en/usage/adding-commands-19","page_id":"/en/usage/adding-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/adding-commands#registering-data-tables","content":"Registered tables appear in the `data` command, input suggestions, and the `Data` tab."},"233":{"id":"/en/usage/adding-commands-20","page_id":"/en/usage/adding-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/adding-commands#writing-output","content":"Use `CommandContext.Output` for leveled output."},"234":{"id":"/en/usage/adding-commands-21","page_id":"/en/usage/adding-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/adding-commands#advanced-iterminalmodule","content":"Use modules when you want to ship a reusable set of related commands."},"235":{"id":"/en/usage/adding-commands-22","page_id":"/en/usage/adding-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/adding-commands#advanced-iterminalmodule","content":"For in-game cheat and debug commands, `RegisterCommand(...)` is usually enough."},"236":{"id":"/en/usage/adding-commands-23","page_id":"/en/usage/adding-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/adding-commands#advanced-iterminalmodule","content":"Implement `ITerminalModule` and install it once with `InstallModule()`."},"237":{"id":"/en/usage/adding-commands-24","page_id":"/en/usage/adding-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/adding-commands#advanced-iterminalmodule","content":"Install it after bootstrap:"},"238":{"id":"/en/usage/adding-commands-25","page_id":"/en/usage/adding-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/adding-commands#advanced-iterminalmodule","content":"Next: Command Reference"},"239":{"id":"/en/usage/cheat-hud","page_id":"/en/usage/cheat-hud","type":"page","content":"Cheat HUD","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Usage"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/usage/cheat-hud"},"240":{"id":"/en/usage/cheat-hud-0","page_id":"/en/usage/cheat-hud","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/usage/cheat-hud#opening-it","content":"Opening it"},"241":{"id":"/en/usage/cheat-hud-1","page_id":"/en/usage/cheat-hud","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/usage/cheat-hud#layout","content":"Layout"},"242":{"id":"/en/usage/cheat-hud-2","page_id":"/en/usage/cheat-hud","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/usage/cheat-hud#open--close-listeners","content":"Open / close listeners"},"243":{"id":"/en/usage/cheat-hud-3","page_id":"/en/usage/cheat-hud","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/usage/cheat-hud#how-entries-are-listed","content":"How entries are listed"},"244":{"id":"/en/usage/cheat-hud-4","page_id":"/en/usage/cheat-hud","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/usage/cheat-hud#behavior","content":"Behavior"},"245":{"id":"/en/usage/cheat-hud-5","page_id":"/en/usage/cheat-hud","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/usage/cheat-hud#dock-and-shortcuts","content":"Dock and shortcuts"},"246":{"id":"/en/usage/cheat-hud-6","page_id":"/en/usage/cheat-hud","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/usage/cheat-hud#parameter-forms-and-execution","content":"Parameter forms and execution"},"247":{"id":"/en/usage/cheat-hud-7","page_id":"/en/usage/cheat-hud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/cheat-hud","content":"Every cheat registered on the terminal can be run from a **full-screen UI Toolkit HUD**.\nRegistering a command is all it takes: the HUD picks it up automatically."},"248":{"id":"/en/usage/cheat-hud-8","page_id":"/en/usage/cheat-hud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/cheat-hud#opening-it","content":"Gesture"},"249":{"id":"/en/usage/cheat-hud-9","page_id":"/en/usage/cheat-hud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/cheat-hud#opening-it","content":"Action"},"250":{"id":"/en/usage/cheat-hud-10","page_id":"/en/usage/cheat-hud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/cheat-hud#opening-it","content":"Editor / desktop"},"251":{"id":"/en/usage/cheat-hud-11","page_id":"/en/usage/cheat-hud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/cheat-hud#opening-it","content":"**Tap with 3 fingers, 3 times**"},"252":{"id":"/en/usage/cheat-hud-12","page_id":"/en/usage/cheat-hud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/cheat-hud#opening-it","content":"Open / close the cheat HUD"},"253":{"id":"/en/usage/cheat-hud-13","page_id":"/en/usage/cheat-hud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/cheat-hud#opening-it","content":"`F1` / `F10`"},"254":{"id":"/en/usage/cheat-hud-14","page_id":"/en/usage/cheat-hud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/cheat-hud#opening-it","content":"**Tap with 4 fingers, 3 times**"},"255":{"id":"/en/usage/cheat-hud-15","page_id":"/en/usage/cheat-hud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/cheat-hud#opening-it","content":"Show / hide the top-right `Terminal / F2` handle"},"256":{"id":"/en/usage/cheat-hud-16","page_id":"/en/usage/cheat-hud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/cheat-hud#opening-it","content":"`F9`"},"257":{"id":"/en/usage/cheat-hud-17","page_id":"/en/usage/cheat-hud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/cheat-hud#opening-it","content":"Tap the handle"},"258":{"id":"/en/usage/cheat-hud-18","page_id":"/en/usage/cheat-hud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/cheat-hud#opening-it","content":"Open / close the console"},"259":{"id":"/en/usage/cheat-hud-19","page_id":"/en/usage/cheat-hud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/cheat-hud#opening-it","content":"`F2` / `` ` ``"},"260":{"id":"/en/usage/cheat-hud-20","page_id":"/en/usage/cheat-hud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/cheat-hud#opening-it","content":"In the editor the `Tools > Cheat Terminal` menu does the same thing - use it when the Game view\ndoes not have focus and the keys never reach the game."},"261":{"id":"/en/usage/cheat-hud-21","page_id":"/en/usage/cheat-hud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/cheat-hud#layout","content":"The HUD covers the **whole screen** by default. Every row is a comfortable touch target\n(104px minimum) with text sized to match."},"262":{"id":"/en/usage/cheat-hud-22","page_id":"/en/usage/cheat-hud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/cheat-hud#layout","content":"Content is padded by `Screen.safeArea`, so notches and home indicators never cover a row."},"263":{"id":"/en/usage/cheat-hud-23","page_id":"/en/usage/cheat-hud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/cheat-hud#layout","content":"Wide screens (landscape, tablets, the editor Game view) split the list into two or three\ncolumns automatically."},"264":{"id":"/en/usage/cheat-hud-24","page_id":"/en/usage/cheat-hud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/cheat-hud#layout","content":"The bottom status bar carries a large `CLOSE` button, for when the `X` in the header is out\nof thumb reach on a tall phone."},"265":{"id":"/en/usage/cheat-hud-25","page_id":"/en/usage/cheat-hud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/cheat-hud#layout","content":"Prefer the old narrow panel that slides in from the left? Turn full screen off."},"266":{"id":"/en/usage/cheat-hud-26","page_id":"/en/usage/cheat-hud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/cheat-hud#open--close-listeners","content":"The game keeps running behind the HUD and the console. Subscribe to the open/close state to\ndrop `Time.timeScale`, block input, or anything else."},"267":{"id":"/en/usage/cheat-hud-27","page_id":"/en/usage/cheat-hud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/cheat-hud#open--close-listeners","content":"If all you need is to stop time, it is one line. The time scale in effect when the HUD opens is\nsaved and restored on close."},"268":{"id":"/en/usage/cheat-hud-28","page_id":"/en/usage/cheat-hud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/cheat-hud#open--close-listeners","content":"Unsubscribe with `-=`. The views raise the same events directly:\n`CheatHudView.OnOpened` / `OnClosed` / `OnVisibilityChanged`, and the identically named\nevents on `UGuiTerminalView`."},"269":{"id":"/en/usage/cheat-hud-29","page_id":"/en/usage/cheat-hud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/cheat-hud#how-entries-are-listed","content":"Commands are grouped by `category`; the built-in `System` category is always sorted last."},"270":{"id":"/en/usage/cheat-hud-30","page_id":"/en/usage/cheat-hud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/cheat-hud#how-entries-are-listed","content":"The search box at the top filters by name, description and category."},"271":{"id":"/en/usage/cheat-hud-31","page_id":"/en/usage/cheat-hud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/cheat-hud#how-entries-are-listed","content":"The `usage` string decides how a cheat runs."},"272":{"id":"/en/usage/cheat-hud-32","page_id":"/en/usage/cheat-hud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/cheat-hud#how-entries-are-listed","content":"usage"},"273":{"id":"/en/usage/cheat-hud-33","page_id":"/en/usage/cheat-hud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/cheat-hud#how-entries-are-listed","content":"HUD behavior"},"274":{"id":"/en/usage/cheat-hud-34","page_id":"/en/usage/cheat-hud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/cheat-hud#how-entries-are-listed","content":"`god` (no arguments)"},"275":{"id":"/en/usage/cheat-hud-35","page_id":"/en/usage/cheat-hud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/cheat-hud#how-entries-are-listed","content":"Press Run"},"276":{"id":"/en/usage/cheat-hud-36","page_id":"/en/usage/cheat-hud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/cheat-hud#how-entries-are-listed","content":"`gold <amount>`"},"277":{"id":"/en/usage/cheat-hud-37","page_id":"/en/usage/cheat-hud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/cheat-hud#how-entries-are-listed","content":"Enter amount, then Run"},"278":{"id":"/en/usage/cheat-hud-38","page_id":"/en/usage/cheat-hud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/cheat-hud#how-entries-are-listed","content":"`heal [amount]`"},"279":{"id":"/en/usage/cheat-hud-39","page_id":"/en/usage/cheat-hud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/cheat-hud#how-entries-are-listed","content":"Leave amount blank or enter it, then Run"},"280":{"id":"/en/usage/cheat-hud-40","page_id":"/en/usage/cheat-hud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/cheat-hud#behavior","content":"The HUD subscribes to `Terminal.Registry.Changed`, so commands added or removed at runtime\nshow up right away."},"281":{"id":"/en/usage/cheat-hud-41","page_id":"/en/usage/cheat-hud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/cheat-hud#behavior","content":"Results go to the terminal console output and to the status line at the bottom of the HUD."},"282":{"id":"/en/usage/cheat-hud-42","page_id":"/en/usage/cheat-hud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/cheat-hud#behavior","content":"While closed the panel is `display: none`, so it costs nothing to render or lay out, and the\nroot element never intercepts gameplay input."},"283":{"id":"/en/usage/cheat-hud-43","page_id":"/en/usage/cheat-hud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/cheat-hud#behavior","content":"The `Terminal / F2` button in the header opens the full terminal console."},"284":{"id":"/en/usage/cheat-hud-44","page_id":"/en/usage/cheat-hud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/cheat-hud#dock-and-shortcuts","content":"The terminal bootstraps automatically in the editor and development builds. A developer dock is visible at the top right: the sliders icon opens Cheat Library and the terminal icon opens Terminal. Drag the grip or either icon to move the dock within the safe area."},"285":{"id":"/en/usage/cheat-hud-45","page_id":"/en/usage/cheat-hud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/cheat-hud#dock-and-shortcuts","content":"`F1` opens Cheat Library, `F2` opens Terminal, `F10` is another cheat shortcut, and `F9` toggles the dock. Backquote only opens Terminal; Escape closes the active surface."},"286":{"id":"/en/usage/cheat-hud-46","page_id":"/en/usage/cheat-hud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/cheat-hud#parameter-forms-and-execution","content":"Parameter fields are always visible. Enter values and press Run or Enter; you never need to type the command name. `<amount>` is required, `[amount]` is optional, `<x> <y> <z>` creates separate coordinate fields, and `<on|off>` adds choice buttons. Required fields must be filled. Optional fields can be omitted from the end, without gaps. `[args]` and `<text...>` accept several space-separated arguments; quote a single value that contains spaces."},"287":{"id":"/en/usage/cheat-hud-47","page_id":"/en/usage/cheat-hud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/cheat-hud#parameter-forms-and-execution","content":"Use category buttons and search to find commands. Values survive filtering, resizing and reopening. Results and errors appear on the card, bottom status bar and terminal output. Switching surfaces closes the previous surface."},"288":{"id":"/en/usage/commands","page_id":"/en/usage/commands","type":"page","content":"Command Reference","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Usage"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/usage/commands"},"289":{"id":"/en/usage/commands-0","page_id":"/en/usage/commands","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/usage/commands#built-in-commands","content":"Built-in commands"},"290":{"id":"/en/usage/commands-1","page_id":"/en/usage/commands","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":